      "problem": "What is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$\n\n- The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Its zeros occur at $x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},….$\n\n- Its maximum values occur at $0,\\pm 2\\pi ,…$\n\n- Its minimum values occur at $\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 3\\pi ,…$\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254255/assets/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)",
